                    sum_r3_nothreshold:     `Never set a threshold — the model changes no decision.`,
                    sum_r3_accuracy:        `Tuned the threshold for accuracy, not cost-weighted value.`,
                    sum_r3_weak:            `Threshold or deployment design partly tuned.`,
                    sum_r4_good:            `Led with lift and the peso; absorbed the shock with discipline.`,
                    sum_r4_accuracy:        `Reported accuracy/architecture to a board that buys lift.`,
                    sum_r4_weak:            `Defense or shock response under-tuned.`,

                    insight_lift:           `Lift proven: you framed the most valuable problem as a decision, deployed a model that shipped inside the window, set the cost-weighted threshold that turns predictions into pesos, and defended it as lift. The board funds the next phase — data science earned its mandate.`,
                    insight_notdeployed:    `Notebook, not production: you chased the marginal 7 points of accuracy with a model that needed 14 weeks against a 90-day window. On day 90 you had a brilliant model and nothing live — and a deployed 82% would have beaten your undeployed 89%. The board concluded data science cannot ship.`,
                    insight_nothreshold:    `No decision changed: you optimised the model but never set the deployment threshold, so the predictions sat unused and shifted no dispatch decisions. A model that changes no decision creates no value — the threshold, not the model, produces the outcome.`,
                    insight_wrongproblem:   `The convenient problem: you solved the cleanest-data problem rather than the most valuable decision, and even a good model on a low-value target could not clear the board’s lift bar. Problem selection is a portfolio decision, not a data-convenience default.`,
                    insight_accuracythreshold: `Accuracy, not value: you tuned the threshold to maximize overall accuracy while a false negative cost 4.5× a false positive — so the value-maximizing pesos were left on the table. With asymmetric error costs, the accuracy-max threshold is rarely the value-max one.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed result: parts of the pipeline landed — framing, model, threshold — but they did not fully reinforce each other, so the lift fell short of the bar the board set. Decision-first analytics needs every link in the chain to hold.`,
                    insight_reportedaccuracy: `You shipped real lift but reported it as accuracy: leading the board with AUC or architecture instead of the two-point drop worth ₱70M risks the next round of funding — the board buys decision lift and pesos, not model metrics.`,
                    insight_nomonitoring:   `One-time deployment: you shipped without drift monitoring or a rollback plan, so when traffic patterns shift the model degrades silently until cancellations climb back. Production analytics needs a leading metric and a rollback, not a launch and a victory lap.`,
                    insight_nobaseline:     `No measurement design: without a live A/B test or holdout you cannot prove the model <em>caused</em> the lift, so only part of the value is credible to the board. Lift is a causal claim — earn it against a baseline.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `Over budget: the build cost more than the ₱90M the board authorised, eroding the net value even where the lift was real. The accuracy-versus-cost trade-off includes the cost.`,
                    insight_deployedwins:   `The defining lesson held: a model that deploys in time and acts on a value-tuned threshold beats a more accurate one that misses the window. The board pays for deployed lift, not for AUC in a notebook.`,

                    hint_notdeployed:       `Your chosen build misses the 90-day window — on day 90 you will have nothing live and zero lift. Re-scope to a model that deploys in time; a deployed 82% beats an undeployed 89%.`,
                    hint_nothreshold:       `You have not set a decision threshold, so the model changes no dispatch decision and creates no value. Choose the cost-weighted threshold before the next round.`,
                    hint_wrongproblem:      `You are solving the cleanest-data problem, not the most valuable one — even a strong model here cannot clear the board’s lift bar. The valuable decision is the 14% cancellation rate.`,
                    hint_accuracythreshold: `Your threshold maximizes accuracy, but a ₱180 false negative dwarfs a ₱40 false positive — recompute it to maximize value and let it move below 50%.`,
                    hint_nomonitoring:      `You have no drift monitoring or rollback — silent degradation will erode your lift in production. Add a leading metric and a rollback trigger.`,
                    hint_reportedaccuracy:  `You are framing the result as accuracy or architecture; the board buys decision lift and pesos. Re-state it as the operating-metric move and its ₱-value.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — real lift, deployed in time, value-tuned. Land it: defend the result as decision lift and pesos, and keep the monitoring honest.`,

